  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important question is whether a multimodal fusion of RNA and image features provides a meaningful accuracy advantage over single-modality baselines, and what a reasonable 'strong default' performance looks like. config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is chosen because: (1) it tests the core multimodal hypothesis with two well-established, pretrained representations (PCA for RNA, ViT-L for images) that require no additional encoder training; (2) avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion are the simplest, lowest-risk choices, reducing the chance of a poor result due to architectural complexity; (3) it serves as a strong baseline against which I can later compare learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), transformer aggregation, and concat fusion. Expected relative cost: medium — ViT-L forward passes dominate, but the absence of a transformer aggregation layer and a learned RNA encoder keeps training time well below the most expensive configs (e.g., those with transformer + scgpt). This leaves ample GPU budget for the remaining 9 experiments to explore more complex variants."
}

